  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Government of Timor-Leste Capacity for Disaster Management &#x2013; Logistical Support for Incident Command System Training in Timor-Leste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project facilitated by IOM on behalf the United States Forest Service aims to strengthen the capacity of the Timor Leste Government and first responders to establish an effective emergency management system that is used by all levels of government &#x2013;national, municipality, and community &#x2013; to enhance operations and coordination before, during and after natural or man-made disasters. The project primarily provides training to the Ministry of Interior, Secretary of State Civil Protection including the National Disaster Risk Management Directorate, fire fighters, and other first responders to create a common language for coordination among entities for effective and efficient emergency management system as they prepare for, respond to emergencies.</narrative>
  </description>
